    (CJIC), and MSP has not been asked about them. SEMCOG's open-data portal
    carries a Copyright License Agreement covering everything it publishes
    (https://maps-semcog.opendata.arcgis.com/pages/copyright-license-agreement):
    a perpetual, royalty-free licence to reproduce, modify and publish; the
    REQUIRED copyright notice reproduced above, which since 2026-09-20 is
    printed on the Safe streets panel itself as well as here (the panel also
    names SEMCOG and the State Police); a one-way clause under which the user indemnifies
    SEMCOG; and a clause granting no third-party rights, which is why MSP's
    position matters. The layer is read by hand about once a year and kept as
    counts only, and both bodies are named on the panel. Open for Kyle: accept
    the agreement including its indemnification clause knowingly, or remove the
    layer. If SEMCOG or MSP objects the layer is deleted and the panel
    disappears.


THE ELEVEN TRANSPORT LAYERS ON THE MAP

Each layer names its owner and its licence text on the Map tab and in
data/ingested/transit/source.json. Nothing is drawn from a tile server and no
layer owner is contacted while the map is open.

  City of Detroit open data (data.detroitmi.gov) — the portal publishes a
    disclaimer and no licence grant:
      DDOT Bus Routes; DDOT Bus Stops; QLine Stops (M-1 RAIL); MoGo Stations;
      Bike Lanes (Department of Public Works)
    DDOT also publishes a GTFS feed its portal marks CC0. We cannot read it:
    detroitmi.gov answers 403 to scripts and we do not disguise a request.
  SMART, published GTFS feed (routes and stops) — no terms published
  Detroit People Mover, published GTFS feed (stations) — no terms published
  Michigan Department of Transportation, Carpool Lots (park and ride) —
    a disclaimer, no redistribution limit stated
  US DOT Bureau of Transportation Statistics, NTAD Amtrak Stations —
    a work of the United States government, unrestricted public use
  US DOT Bureau of Transportation Statistics, NTAD Intercity Bus Atlas Stops —
    CC BY-NC 4.0 (attribution, non-commercial).
    Licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
    Modified: filtered to Detroit, Hamtramck, Highland Park and Dearborn plus a
    surrounding margin, and reduced to the fields the app draws. 9 stops of the
    national file. data/ingested/transit/intercity_bus.json is NOT covered by
    this repository's Apache-2.0 licence (data/LICENSE-DATA.md).


PLACES WE LINK TO, AND TAKE NOTHING FROM

  313SafeBeds (313safebeds.com) — real-time shelter status. Its page was read
    in a browser; the shelter screen opens with a link to it and copies nothing.
  Transit (transitapp.com) — the "Bus directions in the Transit app" button uses
    Transit's own documented URL scheme and passes only a destination. Their
    developer page states no terms and no branding rule, so we use the plain
    word "Transit" in text, no logo, no asset of theirs, and fetch nothing from
    their servers. Asking them what they want is still owed.
  DDOT and SMART trip planners, and the public application sites behind the
    link-outs on several need screens. Named as theirs; never an endorsement of
    ours, and none of them endorses us.


FORMATS AND STANDARDS
